      "created_time_dt": "2026-11-21T12:39:16.122776",
      "desc": "**Kubernetes Pods** configured with `hostNetwork: true` are identified, meaning they share the node's network namespace and use the host's IP stack, interfaces, and ports.",
      "title": "Pod does not use hostNetwork",
      "types": [],
      "uid": "prowler-kubernetes-core_minimize_hostNetwork_containers-kind-demo-namespace: kube-system-kindnet-nvsmq"
    },
    "resources": [
      {
        "group": {
          "name": "core"
        },
        "labels": [],
        "name": "kindnet-nvsmq",
        "namespace": "kube-system",
        "type": "Pod",
        "uid": "4bac9bc1-e190-41bd-a393-bcb5a1e2ab5c"
      }
    ],
    "category_name": "Findings",
    "category_uid": 2,
    "class_name": "Detection Finding",
    "class_uid": 2004,
    "remediation": {
      "desc": "Disallow `hostNetwork` by default. Enforce **least privilege** with admission policies that block it, allowing narrowly scoped exceptions only for trusted system workloads. Prefer standard pod networking with **NetworkPolicies**, and isolate node services for **defense in depth**.",
      "references": [
        "https://hub.prowler.com/check/core_minimize_hostNetwork_containers"
      ]
    },
    "risk_details": "Using the **host network namespace** exposes node-local interfaces and traffic to the pod. A compromise can enable packet capture and request spoofing (**C/I**), access to node services (e.g., kubelet), and port binding conflicts, causing outages (**A**) and enabling **lateral movement** across the cluster.",
    "time": 1795264756,
    "time_dt": "2026-11-21T12:39:16.122776",
    "type_uid": 200401,
    "type_name": "Detection Finding: Create"
  },
